expert tiers: read misses straight into the host pool instead of into a bytearray that admit then copies again -- every expert was being memcpy'd twice (18.8MB read plus 18.8MB slot copy), so a 40-layer prefill moved ~361GB of bytes on the main thread. py-spy sampled the stack three times and every sample sat in _insert_locked's slot[:] = data, which is the prefill 114s and the 300-1900ms decode steps